criteria.notes:
Everything else in b1 holds on reading and in my checks:
- migrations equal the spec;
- check-node.cjs is flag-free ES5 and every flagged script is prefixed;
- F-TR-17 cap (limits.test.js);
- SEC-5 lengths (16/12/32 bytes) and placeholder refusal;
- loopback base URLs only with RS_TEST_OFFLINE;
- Host allow-list with 421;
- JSON body cap of 65,536 bytes with 413;
- static handler confined by realpath;
- approvalPageCsp exact.
Unmet only because the criterion 'a second process starting at the same time skips applied versions' fails intermittently (PB-1).

findings.detail:
The phase criterion requires every test that proves a criterion or finding to start its name with that id. These do not:
- 'RS_SAGA_LEASE_MS must be at least 3 times RS_PAYPAL_TIMEOUT_MS' (ARCH-26, limits.test.js:40);
- 'RS_MODEL_CUSTOMER_DAILY_SHARE ... (default 0.2)' (SEC-10/OQ-D7, limits.test.js:66);
- 'RS_FAKE_APPROVAL_HOST is 127.0.0.1 outside test mode' (SEC-12, hosts.test.js:116);
- 'RS_TEST_HOOKS is refused when the Sandbox adapter is selected' (secrets.test.js:159);
- 'SQLITE_BUSY after the busy timeout maps to 503 DB_BUSY' (connection.test.js:119; an RS-14-named variant exists in db-busy.test.js);
- 'default deny: a route with a non-public policy answers 401' (ARCH-25, app.test.js:310).
All brief criteria of this phase are fully named. The gap affects only the evidence table's ability to cite design items by id, so it is minor, not major.
